WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.434
-My first guest
is a Golden Globe-winning actor

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:06.267
who stars in the new movie
"The Harder They Fall,"

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.634
which is in theaters now

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.868
and streaming on Netflix
November 3rd.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:13.000
Here is Idris Elba!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.734
Yeah! Oh, wow!

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:16.934
Oh, wow!

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.334
Oh, no! He's rising!

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.801
He's rising! Oh, my God!

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:24.000
-How are you, Jimmy?
It's good to see you.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:26.267
-You're the greatest.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.000
I love that you dressed up,
buddy.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.367
How you doing?

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.434
-I'm great, man.
I didn't dress up.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:32.601
This is me every day, bro.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:33.901
-Oh, well, I apologize.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.934
I hope you take no offense
to that.

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.534
Yeah.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:40.100
I guess you're in
the Halloween spirit, bud.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.200
-Dude, I'm actually deejaying
in 45 minutes at a nightclub.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.100
-Is that right?
-At Annabelle's, so --

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.567
Yeah, so I didn't want to
come on the show like this,

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.701
but just in terms of efficiency,
I had to get there.

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.234
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.534
-Of any show, you know
that you are allowed to --

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.734
you have to do this on my show.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.634
Of any show.
You know, come on, buddy.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.234
We're a family, right?
Yeah.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:02.767
-Yeah.
Shout out to The Roots.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.067
What's up, gentlemen?
-There you go. That's right.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.701
We love you.
We love you, bud.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.801
I love that you did that.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.667
Idris, I want to -- by the way,

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.934
even dressed like this,
you're still sexy, buddy.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.067
That's all I'm gonna say.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.467
-Oh, yeah? Thanks, Jimmy.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:20.067
-Is this a zucchini moment?

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:21.067
-No.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.000
Unfortunately, it's not.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.667
Well, it might be.
I don't know.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:31.067
I do want to ask you -- but
before we get into the movie,

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.367
I have to ask you about working
with Paul McCartney.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:37.267
This is Paul McCartney's
newest album,

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:40.534
and you do a whole remix on it.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.934
And you sound amazing,
by the way.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:44.167
-Aww, thanks man.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.334
-How did you get involved
with this?

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:47.667
Did Paul just call you?

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.567
-No. Did he call me?
No, no.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.434
You know what, I had the
opportunity to be you for a day

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.868
and interview Paul McCartney
for The BBC.

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:57.834
And we're sitting on the sofa,
having a great chat.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.234
And then,
during one of the breaks,

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.534
he tells me about this album
and he says, you know,

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:02.567
"I'm going to remix it.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.334
I'm going to get
a bunch of artists."

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:07.000
And literally, like, a bone
it just fell out my mouth.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.868
I was like, "Let me do one."

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.267
-And then you were like --
-There was a real awkward pause.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.200
-Yeah.
-He was like...

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.601
-He's like, uh...
-"Yeah, sure.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.968
Sure, Idris. Yeah, yeah, sure.
Have a go.

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.400
Have a go, if you like."

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.634
And then I started talking to
him about the stems

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:22.934
and the Pro Tools files.

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:25.501
He was like, "Oh. Okay.
I'll send them to you."

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:26.667
-You know
what you're talking about.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:27.901
It's fantastic.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.934
It might be one of my favorites
on the album.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.601
I was going to ask you --
-Oh, thank you, man.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:32.968
-We have this.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.367
You're doing a song with
Paul McCartney, who is a legend.

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:39.968
I know that you've also deejayed
for Madonna.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.767
I know that you also --
we talked about that.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:45.968
You deejayed the royal wedding,
Prince Harry and Meghan Markle.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.334
These are high-pressure gigs.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.868
Which one is the most stressful?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.434
-The wedding. No doubt.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:55.501
-Really?

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:56.934
-The wedding, yeah.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.567
This wasn't like, you know,
this wasn't like my cousin --

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.534
my cousin's wedding,
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.400
This was like...
-Yeah, yeah. This is --

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.267
-You know, this wasn't
at the community hall.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.567
You know, the reception.

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:10.000
This was like a big, big deal.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.534
You know, they're good friends,
and I wanted to make sure

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:13.534
they had a great time,

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:14.901
so it was a lot of pressure.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:16.300
-Do you know what --
-I mean a lot.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.701
-Do you know what song
you're going to play

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:21.334
when you kick off the party,
or is it...

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.234
-No, but I have a collection
of songs

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.434
that any one of them
could be a good kick-off.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.501
And Meghan had sent me
a playlist,

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.033
so I knew
what she wanted already.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:32.367
-I was -- I wanted to ask you
about this,

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:33.901
because I have an idea.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:37.467
We might have crossed paths
before I even knew you.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.901
Were you a bouncer

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:41.767
at Caroline's Comedy Club
here in Manhattan?

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:44.133
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I used to work at the door.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:47.100
I was upstairs, and then I went
downstairs and watched the show

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.033
and just, you know, made sure
no one misbehaved.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.968
-Did we ever
run into each other?

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:54.601
-Yeah. I saw you.
I saw your show.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.634
It was, you know.
It was all right.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.834
[ Laughter ]
Remember that --

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:03.267
-I was just --
I was just starting out.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.367
I was brand new.
-No, no, no.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:06.701
You used to do that --
Remember that --

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.968
You used to do that Troll skit.

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:11.300
-I did!

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.234
I had a Troll doll bit,
and I would do impressions.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:14.100
Yeah.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.601
-Yeah, it was terrible.

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:17.133
But, you know, people loved it.

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:21.033
-You saw that?
That's crazy, man.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.701
-I was there.
-That's so wild, man.

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.501
I loved Caroline's.
That was one of my favorite --

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:26.968
That was one of my favorite
clubs ever, man.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.567
-Me too. Me too.
-That's wild.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.934
-Nah, you were great, actually.
I do remember, you were great.

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:32.300
And, you know, I --

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.334
Oftentimes, I get brought
into the comedy

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:36.167
'cause I was a English guy.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.033
Black Englishman at the door
at the time

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:40.300
is still a novelty out there
in New York,

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.133
and they used to just roast me
basically all day.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.934
You didn't roast me,
but most of them did.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.701
-Thank you. Yeah, good.
I'm glad I didn't.

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:50.133
But look at you now, bud.
Look at you now.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.300
Now you're in --
-Yeah.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.601
-I love this new movie.
-I'm in "Blacula."

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:56.000
-Yeah. I didn't mean that.
That's correct.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.667
But, also,
you're in a great new movie

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.467
called "The Harder They Fall."

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.467
Jay Z is a producer on this,
as well, by the way.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.834
It's a great cast.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.734
You know,
I love LaKeith Stanfield.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:07.534
He's one of my favorite actors
out there.

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:08.834
Do you want to set up
who you play in the film

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:11.300
and what drew you to this movie?

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.434
-Yeah. No, dude,
I'm really proud of this film.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:16.601
It's an incredible movie.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:18.934
You know, I play Rufus Buck,

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.367
who was a real character,
you know?

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:24.434
Rufus Buck was notorious --
sort of criminal.

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:26.601
And, actually,
the real Rufus Buck

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:28.701
was probably --
excuse me, one second.

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:30.133
Ooh.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.300
-Yeah, that makes it better.
-I couldn't even talk.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.267
-Ah, there you go.
-The real Rufus Buck --

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.534
-That's better.
-He was a --

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.534
He was, you know, a young kid.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.133
He was probably
about 19 years old.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.000
In the movie,
we depict him a lot older.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.234
But he was notorious.

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:45.234
And all of the criminals
in the film,

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:46.801
you know, from Trudy Smith,

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:49.701
you know, LaKeith Stanfield
plays Cherokee Bill.

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:52.467
Cherokee Bill,
these are all real characters.

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:54.200
And so, this film not only --

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.067
I mean, it's a piece of fiction,
but it really does lean into

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:59.868
some real characters
that existed, you know?

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:03.000
-I do love a good Western, too.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.834
And I know
you're on the horse a lot.

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.968
And I heard
that you realized on set

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:10.000
that you were allergic
to horses.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.100
-Yeah, yeah.
-That sounds like fun.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:16.033
-No. It was [bleep]
horrible Excuse my language.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:17.567
It was horrible.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:19.400
-I mean, you know,
interesting thing about --

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.634
-That is a nightmare.

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:22.267
What are you supposed to do?

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:24.901
It's a Western.
You got to be on a horse.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:27.667
-Yeah, you know -- you know --
and now I know why

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:30.100
all cowboys did that
squinty-eyes thing.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.200
Their eyes were bleeding,
basically.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.901
And there was this old gentleman

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:39.467
who was one of
the supporting artists.

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:42.133
And he saw me sneezing.
My eyes were red.

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:43.334
And he said to me, "Yo, Idris,

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:46.534
you know, you got to use
some pickle juice."

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:48.767
I was like, "What?"
He's like, "Pickle juice.

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:49.934
You got to drink
some pickle juice.

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:51.033
You're going to be fine."

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:54.267
I was like -- You know,
I had a long,

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:55.501
decent conversation with him.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:57.868
-Try anything, I guess.
-I trusted him, yeah.

00:06:57.868 --> 00:07:00.534
The next day, we -- I drank
some of that pickle juice,

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:01.934
and it actually worked.

00:07:01.934 --> 00:07:03.968
I'm not even going to lie.
-No way.

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:05.667
Pickle juice...
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:07.968
-...helped your allergies?
-Yeah.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:10.234
Completely. I drank
a bunch of pickle juice.

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:11.701
It's something to do
with the dill.

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:12.968
I don't know. Dill.

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.234
-Yeah, man.
-Something to do with dill.

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:15.934
-What's the dill, man?
I love it.

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:18.968
Thank you.
That's so corny.

00:07:18.968 --> 00:07:21.434
People just walked out.
People walked out.

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:23.567
My joke was so corny --
-I like corny jokes.

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:25.033
I like your corny jokes.

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:27.167
Man, when you did them at
Caroline's, they were great.

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:29.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:34.133
-Idris, I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:07:34.133 --> 00:07:36.567
Here's Idris Elba in
"The Harder They Fall."

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.133
Take a look at this.

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:39.467
-Wiley Escoe.

00:07:41.467 --> 00:07:42.634
-Rufus.

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:47.167
♪♪

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:48.868
The world you knew is gone.

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:53.234
There's a flood coming.

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:56.100
Do you think you can hold onto
this place when it hit?

00:07:57.667 --> 00:07:59.801
At least I know enough
to get mine and get out.

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:05.534
Kill me...

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:06.968
and you'll have nothing.

00:08:09.033 --> 00:08:12.767
-You know, a man like you
will have us all subservient

00:08:12.767 --> 00:08:14.734
to the end of our days,

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:17.734
so long as you can buy
yourself a house...

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:19.567
a badge...

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:21.501
and them goddamn gold teeth.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:26.868
♪♪

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:29.033
-You want to do this here?

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:32.701
♪♪

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:34.033
[ Spectators shout ]

00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:36.100
[ Horse whinnying ]

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.767
-Come on.
That's a star, right there.

00:08:38.767 --> 00:08:40.667
That's a star!
I love you, buddy!

00:08:40.667 --> 00:08:41.968
"The Harder They Fall"...
-Thank you, bro.

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:43.200
-...is in theaters now

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.534
and streaming on Netflix
November 3rd.

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.033
When we come back, Idris and I

00:08:47.033 --> 00:08:48.801
are going head-to-head
in a new game.

00:08:48.801 --> 00:08:49.968
Stick around.
It'll be fun.

